# Tab containers (src/chrome/browser/containers/): each container is a storage partition, and a
# tab stays in the partition its WebContents starts in, so the browser only has to start tabs in
# the right one. These are the hooks both browsers share; the browser target is the product's
# //chrome/browser/containers/platform (see containers_platform.h).
# - web_contents_impl.cc: a window a container's page opens without an opener (target=_blank,
#   noopener) stays in the container; content gives such a window a new default SiteInstance.
# - navigation_entry_impl.cc: a page's committed partition, which the session handler saves as
#   the page's extended info: the public NavigationEntry doesn't tell its SiteInstance.
# - permission_util.cc: notifications work in containers; Chromium blocks them in a partition
#   that isn't the site's own.
# - chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc: the service, created with each regular
#   profile, with its prefs and the session handler.
# - chrome_content_browser_client_navigation_throttles.cc: Traffic Control's throttle.
